<resources>

    <!-- TEMPORARY - remove together with this whole values-v35 folder in the 2.0 rewrite.

         Android 15 (API 35) draws apps that target it edge to edge: the activity window
         extends behind the status and navigation bars, and Window.setStatusBarColor stops
         having any effect. Every XML screen in this app was laid out before that, so it
         would need real WindowInsets handling to look right.

         This flag asks the platform to keep the pre Android 15 behaviour. It is deprecated
         from the day it was introduced and Google has said it will stop working in a
         future Android release, so it buys time - it is not a solution. Handling insets
         properly is a 2.0 task, tracked in UPGRADE-NOTES.md. -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="BaseAppTheme">
        <item name="android:windowOptOutEdgeToEdgeEnforcement">true</item>
    </style>

</resources>
